# Prerequisites

**Prerequisites:** none.
**You will learn:** what this manual assumes and what it will not teach.
**Time:** two minutes.
**Next:** [Install Rocci](/docs/start/install/).

This manual is for programmers who are new to Rocci. It does not teach
programming from zero.

## Required

| You can | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Read typed code and use a terminal | Every tutorial runs commands |
| Use Git | The documented install path is a source checkout |
| Edit a text file | You will inspect `.rocci` modules |

## Toolchain (installed in the next page)

| Tool | Role | As tested |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Rust and Cargo | Build the Rocci workspace | GitHub Actions `dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable`, edition 2024 crates |
| Roc nightly | Compile generated and authored Roc | `nightly-2026-08-10` (`7df8509`), pinned in `docker/install-roc.sh` |
| Native webview | Preview window | macOS WebKit, Linux WebKitGTK 4.1, Windows system webview |

A mismatched Roc nightly can reject syntax that is valid for this repository.

## Optional refreshers

- [Roc for Rocci authors](/docs/start/roc-for-rocci/) — modules, records, tags, `match`, effects, `?`.
- [Web foundations for Roc authors](/docs/start/web-foundations/) — semantic HTML, HTTP, fragments, SSE.
- Full Roc language: [roc-lang.org](https://www.roc-lang.org/).
- HTML and HTTP: MDN and the HTTP specifications. This manual teaches only the
  subset later examples need.

## Platforms

| Platform | Documentation claim |
| --- | --- |
| macOS | Verified in CI (`macos-latest`) |
| Linux | Verified in CI (`ubuntu-latest`) with WebKitGTK 4.1 |
| Windows | Development runs use the OS webview; packaging is not implemented; not in the CI matrix |

Continue with [installation](/docs/start/install/).
